# Slice 297 probe (FORMAL-DEFAULT-FORMS; the book provenance :498, :699; Codex 293 and 296 reviews: an already formed
# Structure in the default's position is taken by the formal's general contract): a Structure formal whose written default
# names a Structure (`T: p D`).  A call without the argument takes D; one with T takes T.  Entry 7; a wrong value leaves
# as the exit code (v, then 100 + v).
T:
    int: a 1
end: T
D:
    int: a 4
end: D
fn: f (T: p D) int
    return: p\a
end: f
int: code 7
int: v f()
if: v != 4
    code: v
---
if: code = 7 && f(T) != 1
    code: 100 + f(T)
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
